The projection of $\mathbf{a}$ onto $\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\frac{\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}}{\|\mathbf{b}\|^2}$ times $\mathbf{b}.$  For this problem,
\[\frac{\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 3 \\ z \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}}{\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}} = \frac{12}{35}.\]This gives
\[\frac{-30-5z+3z}{31} = \frac{12}{35} \quad\Longrightarrow\quad -3z = \frac{552}{35} \quad\Longrightarrow\quad z = \boxed{-\frac{184}{35}}.\]. The answer is -\frac{184}{35}
